abstract: >-
  Automated Version Control is a process for tracking
  changes to files and folders within a "repository". This
  workshop will teach you how to use the Git version control
  system to manage your code, tracking changes to files,
  inspecting and merging multiple different changes, and how
  to collaborate with other Git users using the GitHub
  online respository store.
